# Merge rules (deploy safety audit 2026-10-27,
# docs/dev/DEPLOY_SAFETY_AUDIT_2026-10-27.md, part «Конфликты»).
#
# merge=union: git keeps the lines of BOTH sides instead of a conflict.
# Only for files where every line is independent and order does not matter
# (an append-only list). Never for JSON/TS/YAML (union can break syntax or
# keep two versions of one entry). Honoured by `git merge` on a machine
# (our union branches are merged locally); GitHub's own merge button ignores
# it, so the PR may still show "conflicts" until the branch is merged locally.
packages/api-contract/oasdiff-err-ignore.txt merge=union

# Generated files: collapsed in PR diffs. On a conflict take either side and
# re-run the generator (docs/dev/SHARED_REGISTRIES.md): `npm run contract:fast`
# for the contract, `npm run db:erd:fast --workspace apps/api` for the ERD.
packages/api-contract/openapi.json linguist-generated=true
packages/api-contract/dart/lib/** linguist-generated=true
docs/db/ERD.md linguist-generated=true
